= World Wide Web =

== Overview ==
The '''World Wide Web''' is an information system of interrelated resources identified by URIs and accessed through Web protocols and representations.

The Web commonly operates over the Internet, but it is not the Internet itself. Web architecture centers on identification of resources, interaction between agents and resources, and representations transferred between them.

Browsers and servers are common Web agents. HTTP and URIs are foundational Web technologies, while many other Internet services do not use the Web.

== Boundaries ==
* World Wide Web ≠ Internet
* Web ≠ HTTP alone
* Web resource ≠ physical file necessarily

